From 6b095635bb367f1cab423fe13136180cc6f54ee2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ravindra Lakkireddy <85186928+rlakki08@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 20:38:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] feat(parts): made to size -- POST /parts/{id}/resize
 rebuilds a part's model at a new W x H x D

For the headset's Size & finish panel (width / height / depth steppers, "Fit to opening"). New
server/resize.py builds the model the way its tier made model.glb:

- llm: the template plan resolve_asset cached (asked with the part's own size: a cache hit, no
  LLM call) built again at the new size -- frame members, sashes and panes keep their proportions
  -- with the product photo on the same face. ~0.1 s.
- proxy: the photo decal box at the new size; cad / scad / ai_mesh: model.glb stretched per axis
  about its mount-face origin (`scaled`).
- `finish`: F11 first (finish.apply, Imagine, cached); its variant photo and colours go on the
  rebuilt model (finish.build gains `dims`). A tint-only finish is left to the headset
  (`finish_source: "tint"`).
- Each size is built once: model-size-<w>x<h>x<d>[-<finish>].glb (served by the model-{slug}.glb
  route) with its reply in a .json beside it. 409 while model.glb is still being made; 422 outside
  0.5-2x the listing or under 10 mm.
- finish.product_roles keeps glass (KEEP_ROLES): a window's panes are its largest role and were
  taken for the product colour, so a bronze window got bronze glass.

Live on :8007: a Jeld-Wen 59.5 x 47.5 in slider at 1487 x 1187 x 83 mm -> template in 0.10 s (cached
0.00 s); + Bronze -> Imagine $0.07, 8.1 s.

